  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 335 AM EDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nThe long term forecast period opens up Monday with the midlevel \ntrough extending across the Ohio and Tennessee Valleys beginning to \ncutoff. This weak cutoff low will slowly meander northeastward on \nTuesday before being reabsorbed into the main flow across the Great \nLakes by Wednesday. As such, at least isolated to widely scattered \nPoPs can be expected each day given the proximity of this feature, \nthough coverage will be markedly lower than the widespread weekend \nactivity. \n\nBy late week, we transition into a more typical summer pattern \ncharacterized by broad midlevel \"dirty\" ridging. As such, typical \nsummertime weather can be anticipated through the end of the week \nwith diurnally-enhanced scattered showers and thunderstorms during \nthe afternoon and evening.\n\nInitial \"cooler\" high temperatures Monday and Tuesday will bring \nmore widespread 80s to low 90s. Temperatures will be on a gradual \nwarming trend, however, with highs in the 90s increasingly \ncommonplace by mid-to-late week next week.",
